## Quality Assurance Enforcement

### Strict QA Standards
- **NEVER** lower or disable coverage thresholds
- **NEVER** skip tests or mark them as pending without justification
- **ALWAYS** write tests before or alongside code (TDD preferred)
- **ALWAYS** ensure tests pass before committing
- **ALWAYS** maintain minimum 80% coverage across all metrics
- **REJECT** PRs that do not meet coverage requirements
- **REQUIRE** test coverage for all new features and bug fixes

### Coverage Enforcement in CI/CD
- Coverage thresholds are enforced in GitHub Actions
- PRs cannot be merged if coverage is below 80%
- Coverage reports are generated and uploaded to Codecov
- Coverage trends are monitored and must not decrease

### Test Quality Standards
- Tests must be meaningful and test actual behavior
- Tests must be independent and not rely on execution order
- Tests must be fast (< 100ms per test when possible)
- Tests must be maintainable and readable
- Tests must cover edge cases and error scenarios

